		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3781&amp;p=29510#p29510"><![CDATA[
Just a note that in the current Alpha verison the external speaker connections don't seem to work.<br><br>I've bought a RT-82 external speaker mic adaptor, which I ordered from AliExpress<br><br><a href="https://www.aliexpress.com/item/1005005673577923.html" class="postlink">https://www.aliexpress.com/item/1005005673577923.html</a><br><br>And I just tested it with the official firmware, and it seems to work, albeit with some strange effects, but it does not work with the OpenGD77 firmware yet.<br><br>When I plug a normal speaker mic into the adaptor, the official firmware makes some beeps, which indicates it has detected the external speaker mic.<br><br>I dissassembled the adaptor and there is a small PCB with various components including a transistor.<br><br>I presume that there is a sense input into the STM32 MCU from the connector, but at the moment I don't know whether this is correct or which pin is the input, and I don't know how to switch the audio amplifier output to the external speaker connection<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Wed Feb 14, 2024 10:53 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
